# Con Floor Nav

Offline-first Vite + React + TypeScript PWA for convention floor maps (Otakon-first).

## Stack

- UI: React 19, `src/App.tsx` + `src/components/*`, styles in `src/App.css`
- Data: Dexie/IndexedDB (`src/db/schema.ts`, `src/db/types.ts`) — no backend DB
- Map: `MapViewer` SVG overlay, aisle A* in `src/lib/pathfinding.ts`
- Party WS: `server/party-server.ts` also serves `dist/` (`npm start`)
- Android: Capacitor (`capacitor.config.ts`, `android/`)
- Deploy: Render web service (`render.yaml`) — https://con-floor-nav.onrender.com

## Product rules

- Offline-first: never require network for core map/vendor/photos after cache
- Multi-event + multi-map: booths belong to `floorMapId`; imports/sample replace scoped to active event/map
- Custom tags are global on-device (`localStorage` via `src/lib/tags.ts`)
- Share pin works offline; Live party needs Render (or local `VITE_PARTY_WS_URL`)
- Prefer editing existing files; avoid drive-by refactors and unsolicited markdown

## Where things live

| Concern | Location |
|---------|----------|
| Events / maps UI | Settings → `EventsPanel`, `MapsPanel` |
| Import / sample | Settings → `ImportPanel` |
| Backup v2 | `src/lib/backup.ts`, Settings → `BackupPanel` |
| Details / tags | `VendorPanel` + `TagSelect` |
| Share / party | **Go** tab → `SharePartyPanel` |
| Docs | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/PLAN.md`, `AGENTS.md` |

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev          # Vite LAN
npm run build        # tsc + vite build
npm start            # party server + static dist (Render)
npm run party-server # alias of start for local WS
npm run cap:sync     # build + cap sync android
```
